The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);
if (vc4->hang_state)
    vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the `vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);` function is called before the hang state is freed. If the module is unloaded after a GPU hang, the BO cache attempts to manage still-allocated buffer objects (BOs) that are associated with the hang state, leading to potential errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (vc4->hang_state)
    vc4_free_hang_state(dev, vc4->hang_state);
vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);
```
Reason:
The fix involves moving the call to `vc4_bo_cache_destroy(dev);` after the hang state is freed. This ensures that all allocated buffer objects are properly released before the BO cache is destroyed, preventing errors related to managing still-allocated BOs.

